Now that I'm back into keeping this site updated, I could see that it told a lot about what I did, but I wasn't taking the pause to reflect on the impact of work I've led.

So I've added a new [Work section](/work/) to chronicle measurable outcomes and context behind my platform, performance, and design system work.

The blog shares techniques, tutorials, and implementation details. The Work section complements that with evidence-led outcomes — useful for recruiters or my own navel gazing.

It was also an interesting effort to look back at old project notes, I didn't really notice how much my work has transformed from keeping things running towards leading change.

Anyways, examples include:

- [UNDRR platform transformation](/work/2025/impact-story-undrr-platform-transformation/) — cut median response time in half (0.88s → 0.45s), 20% Azure cost reduction, 51% database latency improvement
- [Editorial efficiency improvements](/work/2025/impact-story-editorial-efficiency/) — saved 120 hours monthly per 100 editors by addressing workflow friction
- [GAR 2025 landing page](/work/2025/impact-story-gar2025-landing/) — 40% engagement lift through outcomes-first storytelling and interactive design
- [EMBL Visual Framework](/work/2019/impact-story-embl-visual-framework/) — design system scaled across 50+ sites serving life sciences research

The [Work section](/work/) is live now. Browse the impact stories, and if you have feedback on the format or want to know more about any project, I'd love to hear it.

